            <div xml:id="d742">

                <pb facs="0698" n="526" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg526"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 341.622a/294</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-23T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 23, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4476. Your 5730, February 21, 7 p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d742-f1"/> I do not
                    wish to enter into further prolonged discussion of <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ausable</hi> case, etc. Before the <pb facs="0699" n="527" xml:id="pg527"/>
                    British reply is received, I am anxious to obtain, as indicated in my mail
                    despatch No. 4520, December 1, an intimation as to the attitude of the British
                    Government in the matter. If there is no hope that the British Government will
                    discontinue their practice on the representations made, I desire to make the
                    arbitration proposal in my despatch No. 4520, before Mr. Balfour replies. Before making this proposal,
                    however, telegraph me your views.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
